{
  "title": "The Night of Eid al-Azhaa (Qurban)",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "The tenth night of Zilhajj is a blessed night since it is one of the four nights that should be advisably spent with acts of worship. At this night, the doors of the heavens are opened. It is also highly recommended to visit the tomb of Imam al-Husayn (a.s.) at this night and to say the supplication that has been previously cited in this book within the rites of Friday nights:\nيَا دَاۤئِمَ الْفَضْلِ عَلَى الْبَرِيَّةِ\nYAA DAA-EMAL FAZLE A’LAL BARIYYATE\nO He Who is continuous in bestowing favor upon the creation!\nيَا بَاسِطَ الْيَدَيْنِ بِالْعَطِيَّةِ\nYAA BAASETAL YADAYNE BIL-A’TIYYATE\nO He Who extends both hands with giving!\nيَا صَاحِبَ الْمَوَاهِبِ السَّنِيَّةِ\nYAA SAAHEBAL MAWAAHEBIS SANIYYATE\nO Owner of magnificent gifts!\nصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّ اٰلِهٖ\nSALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADINW WA AALEHI\nBless Muhammad and his family—\nخَيْرِ الْوَرٰى سَجِيَّةً\nKHAYRIL WARAA SAJIYYATANW\nthe best of mankind in natural disposition—\nوَّ اغْفِرْ لَنَا يَا ذَا الْعُلٰى\nWAGH FIR LANAA YAA ZAL O’LAA\nand forgive us, O Possessor of Exaltation, \nفِي هٰذِهِ الْعَشِيَّةِ\nFEE HAAZEHIL A’SHIYYATE.\non this evening."
}
